# Pathan Mastan Khan — Talent Profile Site

A single-page casting profile: clapperboard intro with your stats, a
contact-sheet style photo gallery, and a booking/contact section.
Plain HTML/CSS/JS — no build step, deploys to Vercel as-is.

## 1. Deploy to Vercel

1. Create a free account at https://vercel.com
2. Put these 3 files (`index.html`, `style.css`, `script.js`) in a GitHub repo,
   or drag-and-drop the folder into a new Vercel project at
   https://vercel.com/new
3. Framework preset: **Other** (no build command needed — it's static).
4. Deploy. You'll get a link like `pathan-mastan-khan.vercel.app` to share.

## 2. Set your private admin link (so only you see the upload button)

The upload button is hidden from everyone by default — visitors just see
your stats and gallery. To unlock it for yourself:

1. Open `script.js` and set your own private passcode:
   ```js
   ADMIN_PASSCODE: "something-only-you-know",
   ```
2. After deploying, visit your site once with `?admin=` and that passcode
   added to the URL, e.g.:
   ```
   https://yoursite.vercel.app/?admin=something-only-you-know
   ```
3. That unlocks the upload button on that browser/device (saved locally),
   and the passcode is scrubbed from the address bar right after. Bookmark
   the plain link (without `?admin=...`) for normal use, and keep the
   admin link private for when you need to add photos.
4. To hide the button again on a device, click **"Exit admin view"** next
   to the upload button.
5. While in admin view, a gold banner appears at the top and a **"How to
   upload"** panel walks you through the steps right on the page — you
   won't need to come back to this README once it's set up.
6. Clicking the **P.M.K.** logo in the top-left always refreshes the page
   (handy after uploading a batch of new photos).

**Note:** like the Cloudinary/JSONBin keys below, this passcode lives in
your public source code, so it's a "keep casual visitors out" measure,
not a strong security barrier. Don't reuse it as a password anywhere else.

## 3. Connect photo uploads (so they save online, for everyone)

Right now the "Upload New Photo(s)" button is wired up but not connected
to anywhere yet — you'll see a note under the button until you finish this.

### Step A — Cloudinary (stores the actual photo files)
1. Sign up free at https://cloudinary.com
2. On your Dashboard, copy your **Cloud Name**.
3. Go to **Settings → Upload → Upload presets → Add upload preset**.
   - Set **Signing Mode** to **Unsigned**.
   - Save, then copy the **preset name**.
4. Open `script.js`, and near the top fill in:
   ```js
   CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME: "your-cloud-name",
   CLOUDINARY_UPLOAD_PRESET: "your-preset-name",
   ```

With just this step done, uploads work and photos are hosted online —
but the list of photos is only remembered in the browser you uploaded
from. To make the gallery the same for every visitor (recommended, since
casting directors will view it from their own device), do Step B too.

### Step B — JSONBin (makes the gallery public/shared)
1. Sign up free at https://jsonbin.io
2. Create a new bin with this starting content: `{"photos": []}`
3. Copy the **Bin ID** (in the URL or bin dashboard).
4. Go to your account → **API Keys**, copy your **X-Access-Key**.
5. In `script.js`, fill in:
   ```js
   JSONBIN_BIN_ID: "your-bin-id",
   JSONBIN_API_KEY: "your-x-access-key",
   ```

**Note on security:** this key is visible in your site's public source code,
same as the Cloudinary preset. That's fine for a small personal site like
this one — worst case, someone could add/remove gallery photos. Don't
reuse this JSONBin account or key for anything sensitive.

6. Push the updated `script.js` to redeploy (Vercel redeploys automatically
   on every push if connected to GitHub, or re-drag the folder otherwise).

## 4. Editing your info

All your stats, phone, email, and location live directly in `index.html` —
search for the `Stats & Contact` and `Call Sheet` sections and edit the text.

## Files
- `index.html` — page structure and content
- `style.css` — all styling (clapperboard hero, contact-sheet gallery, etc.)
- `script.js` — upload logic + config (edit the `CONFIG` block at the top)
